#!/usr/bin/env node
// Writes the generated parts of docs/major-prep/ from the data, so the
// tables can never drift from what the site shows (V5.1 §9 "maintain
// structured source data and automatically generated traceability tables").
//   docs/major-prep/ACADEMIC_EVIDENCE.md      sources, requirements, articulation
//   docs/major-prep/CURRICULUM_AND_COVERAGE.md  Ohlone objectives → site units → lessons → items
// Run: npm run docs:college   (edit src/data/college/ and the catalog, not these files)

import { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { SOURCES, STATUS_LABEL, CHECKED, DISCLAIMER, sourceById } from '../src/data/college/sources.js';
import { OHLONE_COURSES } from '../src/data/college/ohloneCourses.js';
import { OHLONE_DS_AS, TARGET_REQUIREMENTS } from '../src/data/college/requirements.js';
import { ARTICULATION } from '../src/data/college/articulation.js';
import { STUDY_ALIGNMENT, studyCoverage } from '../src/data/college/studyAlignment.js';
import { summarize } from '../src/data/college/validate.js';
import { unitById, courseById } from '../src/data/curriculum/catalog.js';
import { LESSONS, lessonById } from '../src/data/curriculum/lessons/index.js';

const cell = (s) => String(s ?? '—').replace(/\|/g, '\\|').replace(/\n/g, ' ');
const row = (xs) => `| ${xs.map(cell).join(' | ')} |`;
const table = (head, rows) => [row(head), row(head.map(() => '---')), ...rows.map(row)].join('\n');
const TARGET_NAME = { sjsu: 'San José State University — Data Science, B.S.', csueb: 'CSU East Bay — Data Science, B.S.', uc: 'UC options — UC Davis Data Science, B.S.; UC Merced Data Science and Computing, B.S.; UC Data Science Transfer Pathway' };

// ——— ACADEMIC_EVIDENCE.md ———
const s = summarize();
const academic = `# Academic evidence — official requirements and articulation

Generated by \`npm run docs:college\` from \`src/data/college/\` — edit the data, not this file. Validated by \`npm run validate:college\` (in CI).

> ${DISCLAIMER}

All sources were read on **${CHECKED}**. Statuses: **verified-current** (official source for the applicable year: Ohlone 2026–2027 catalog, 2026–2027 ASSIST agreements, Fall 2027 admission pages), **verified-prior-year** (official but older — never shown as current), **candidate** (study match only), **unverified** (no authoritative, dated source). ${s.records} records: ${Object.entries(s.byStatus).map(([k, v]) => `${v} ${k}`).join(', ')}. ${s.articulation} articulation rows, ${s.noArticulation} of them with no Ohlone course articulated.

## How the facts were obtained

- **Ohlone College 2026–2027 catalog** — read in a web browser; the catalog PDFs are refused to scripts (HTTP 403). Course units, prerequisites, advisories, terms and C-ID were copied; descriptions are paraphrased as topic lists.
- **ASSIST** — its API rejects direct requests (HTTP 400 without the app's session headers). Agreements were read through ASSIST's own search page, as a student would. Ohlone → SJSU, CSU East Bay and UC Davis agreements are 2026–2027; for UC Merced the newest agreement ASSIST offered was **2025–2026**, recorded as an earlier year.
- **SJSU** program-specific transfer coursework (page updated Aug 28, 2026; Fall 2027 admission), **CSU East Bay** 2026–2027 catalog, **UC Davis** 2026–2027 General Catalog, **UC Merced** Fall 2027 major-preparation page, **UC Data Science Transfer Pathway** (states no academic year → its expectations are *unverified* for a specific term).
- Not consulted: the Spring 2027 Ohlone class schedule (meeting days, modality, seats). Nothing on the site states them.

## Source register

${table(['Source', 'Institution', 'Academic year', 'Read', 'Kind', 'URL'], SOURCES.map((x) => [x.title, x.institution, x.academicYear ?? 'not stated', x.accessedAt, x.kind, x.url]))}

## Ohlone Data Science, A.S. (2026–2027 catalog)

${table(['Requirement', 'Type', 'Notes', 'Status'], OHLONE_DS_AS.map((r) => [r.sendingCourse ?? r.id.split('.').pop(), r.requirementType, r.notes, STATUS_LABEL[r.status]]))}

### Course records

${table(['Course', 'Title', 'Units', 'Prerequisite', 'Advisory', 'Offered', 'Accepted for credit', 'C-ID'], OHLONE_COURSES.map((c) => [c.code, c.title, c.units, c.prerequisite ?? 'none listed', c.advisory, c.offered, c.transferable, c.cid]))}

Notes: CS-108 lists no prerequisite and names no programming language — the site does not treat it as a C++ course. CS-142 is cross-referenced with CNET-142. STAT-C1000 is not in the Data Science A.S. major list. “Accepted for credit at CSU & UC” means transferable units, not that the course meets a major requirement.

## What each target asks for

${Object.entries(TARGET_REQUIREMENTS).map(([t, recs]) => `### ${TARGET_NAME[t]}

${table(['Receiving requirement', 'Institution', 'Type', 'Year', 'Status', 'Notes'], recs.map((r) => [r.receivingCourse, r.institution, r.requirementType, r.academicYear ?? 'not stated', STATUS_LABEL[r.status], r.notes]))}`).join('\n\n')}

## Articulation matrix (ASSIST)

${Object.entries(ARTICULATION).map(([t, recs]) => `### ${TARGET_NAME[t]}

${table(['University course', 'Ohlone course(s)', 'Group', 'Year', 'Status', 'Notes'], recs.map((a) => [a.receivingCourse, a.sendingCourse ?? 'No course articulated', a.group, a.academicYear, STATUS_LABEL[a.status], a.notes]))}

Source: ${sourceById[recs[0].sourceId].title}${t === 'uc' ? `; ${sourceById['assist-ohlone-ucm-dsc-2025-26'].title}` : ''}.`).join('\n\n')}

## Findings a learner should know

- **SJSU:** CS 46A (Introduction to Programming) is matched by Ohlone **CS-116**, not CS-102; CS 46B by CS-124; MATH 42 by CS-113; MATH 39 by MATH-103. All five SJSU impaction courses for Data Science have an Ohlone match (CS 46B or CS 22A: CS-124, or CS-142/CNET-142).
- **CSU East Bay:** only CS 100 is matched (by CS-102). DATA 105, DATA 130, DATA 205 and STAT 215 have **no Ohlone course articulated** in 2026–2027 — they would be taken after transfer unless CSU East Bay advises otherwise.
- **UC Davis:** calculus articulates **as sequences only** (MATH-101A + 101B; 101B + 101C); STA 035A–C and ECS 032B have no Ohlone match; ECS 020, 036A, 036C are matched by CS-113, CS-102 and CS-124 (UC Davis notes these are not the usual courses for its Data Science majors).
- **UC Merced** (2025–2026 agreement): MATH 024 needs **both** MATH-103 and MATH-104.
- The Ohlone degree is an A.S., **not an AS-T**: no AS-T admission advantage applies.
- Supporting-course guidance on the site is provisional and per target (SJSU: CS-113, MATH-103; UC: MATH-101C, MATH-103); the A.S. needs two, transfer preparation may need more. Confirm with a counselor.
`;
writeFileSync('docs/major-prep/ACADEMIC_EVIDENCE.md', academic);

// ——— CURRICULUM_AND_COVERAGE.md ———
const bodies = {};
for (const l of LESSONS) bodies[l.id] = (await l.load()).default;
const itemsOf = (b) => ({
  independent: b.practice.filter((i) => i.level !== 'scaffolded').map((i) => i.id),
  transfer: [...b.practice, ...b.checkpoint, ...(b.apply?.items ?? [])].filter((i) => i.transfer).map((i) => i.id),
  checkpoint: b.checkpoint.map((i) => i.id),
  apply: (b.apply?.items ?? []).map((i) => i.id),
});

const traceRows = [];
const coverageRows = [];
for (const align of STUDY_ALIGNMENT) {
  const c = OHLONE_COURSES.find((x) => x.code === align.code);
  const cov = studyCoverage(align.code);
  let explained = 0;
  let independent = 0;
  let transfer = 0;
  for (const t of cov.topics) {
    const its = t.lessons.map((l) => itemsOf(bodies[l]));
    if (t.lessons.length) explained += 1;
    if (its.some((x) => x.independent.length)) independent += 1;
    if (its.some((x) => x.transfer.length)) transfer += 1;
    traceRows.push([
      `${c.code}`,
      sourceById[c.source].academicYear,
      c.prerequisite ?? 'none listed',
      t.topic,
      t.units.map((u) => `${u} (${unitById[u].lessons.length ? 'written' : 'outline'})`).join(', ') || 'not covered',
      t.lessons.map((l) => `${l}`).join(', ') || '—',
      t.lessons.flatMap((l) => itemsOf(bodies[l]).checkpoint).join(', ') || '—',
      [...new Set(t.lessons.flatMap((l) => lessonById[l].labs))].join(', ') || '—',
      t.lessons.length ? 'AI draft, awaiting human review' : '—',
      t.status === 'taught' ? `more depth: ${t.units.reduce((n, u) => n + unitById[u].planned.length, 0)} planned titles in these units` : t.status === 'outline' ? 'no lesson written yet' : 'not on this site',
    ]);
  }
  coverageRows.push([c.code, c.title, cov.total, explained, independent, transfer, cov.written, cov.planned, align.readiness.map((r) => courseById[r].title).join(', '), 0]);
}

const lessonRows = LESSONS.map((l) => {
  const b = bodies[l.id];
  const it = itemsOf(b);
  return [l.id, courseById[l.course].title, l.competencies.join(', '), b.practice.length + b.checkpoint.length + (b.apply?.items.length ?? 0) + b.priorCheck.length, it.independent.length, it.transfer.length, l.labs.join(', '), b.python ? 'Python' : '', b.cpp ? 'C++' : '', l.review.status];
});

const curriculum = `# Curriculum and coverage — Ohlone objectives to lessons

Generated by \`npm run docs:college\` from the catalog, the lesson bodies and \`src/data/college/studyAlignment.js\` — edit those, not this file.

**Three different things, reported separately (V5.1 §10):** *coverage* (what this site teaches), *learner mastery* (computed per learner on the device — no population data exist), and *college credit* (never awarded by this site).

**Honest summary.** ${LESSONS.length} lessons are written in all, every one an **AI draft awaiting independent human math review (0 human-reviewed)**. Coverage below is counted per catalog topic: a topic counts as *explained* when at least one written lesson teaches it — one lesson is an introduction, not a semester. The “planned” column shows how much of each mapped unit is still only a title. No Ohlone course is fully covered.

## Coverage by Ohlone course

${table(['Course', 'Title', 'Catalog topics', 'Topics with a written lesson', 'With independent questions', 'With transfer questions', 'Written lessons (mapped units)', 'Planned titles (mapped units)', 'Readiness courses on the site', 'Human-reviewed lessons'], coverageRows)}

Integrated exams or projects that are review-ready: **none** are claimed. Three projects (restaurant waste, weather anomalies, sensor-log cleaning) have graded steps and an editorial rubric; see \`src/data/projects/index.js\`.

## Traceability: catalog topic → site unit → lesson → assessment

${table(['Ohlone course', 'Source year', 'Official prerequisite', 'Catalog topic (paraphrased)', 'Site unit(s)', 'Written lesson(s)', 'Checkpoint item IDs', 'Labs', 'Review status', 'Remaining gap'], traceRows)}

## Written lessons and their assessments

${table(['Lesson', 'Course', 'Competencies', 'Items', 'Independent practice', 'Transfer items', 'Labs', 'Python', 'C++', 'Review'], lessonRows)}

Item answers are recomputed by the unit tests (\`src/data/curriculum/__tests__/curriculum.test.js\`); Python output by \`npm run verify:python\`; C++ by \`npm run verify:cpp\`.
`;
writeFileSync('docs/major-prep/CURRICULUM_AND_COVERAGE.md', curriculum);
console.log('wrote docs/major-prep/ACADEMIC_EVIDENCE.md and docs/major-prep/CURRICULUM_AND_COVERAGE.md');
